y containable before they turn unrecoverable is partially false for label-mediated diagnostic misrouting. I won't dodge that. I route those patients to a no-fault compensation board that reaches the diffusely injured a courthouse never does. Deterrence and compensation are two different goods. I'm answering the irreversibility attack with the compensation good — not pretending containment was clean.\n\nThe falsification condition I'll commit to in plain terms: if a label-mediated harm in a consequential class is irreversible AND its ground-truth variable is genuinely unspecifiable even after the fact — so no seeded probe could ever be built and no compensation board could ever score the injury — then basic-tier monitoring is inadequate and the pre-deployment gate wins on that class. The NEJM analysis of the cost-proxy case cuts toward Safetyist on causal mechanism: researchers there warned that empirical regression on the wrong outcome label misses the causal structure entirely. I take that seriously. But the same paper's fix was itself an observable test — substitute the variable, re-measure, watch the bias appear. That's not a reason to freeze deployment. That's the seeded instrument, already built, already validated on 200 million patients. Name me the class where even that move is impossible, or we're agreeing on the mechanism and arguing only about its reach.",
