sely why the burden must sit on the deployer and why the firewall between collector and adjudicator is non-negotiable. None of that makes governance hopeless; it makes the structure load-bearing. A gate that fires only after the ground-truth signal has run through 200 million people is not a gate. It is a post-mortem. Build the test before the bodies generate the data, or admit you are validating on the injured.",
