  "statement": "I concede that the regulator sets and publicly discloses the drift threshold, not the deployer, and that the audit-triggered board beats the claims-triggered version for harm that shows up in the aggregate numbers. I still hold the pre-deployment gate for the one residual the board is structurally blind to: the label-laundered harm with no aggregate gap, irreversible and unscorable even after the fact. I would contract that gate to nothing on a documented case showing a held-out historical probe carries pre-existing ground-truth signal for a novel proxy on a novel population — and expand it only on a documented case of irreversible harm no probe could score even after the deployment runs.\n\nSkeptic calls the gate \"a drawbridge the incumbents pull up behind them,\" and that charge lands on a real failure mode. Conditional funding and open-ended holds do produce compliance theater that entrenches the well-resourced — the firm with a hundred lawyers clears a vague hold; the startup with three does not. The 2025 OpenAI-NVIDIA deal, with up to $100 billion in committed compute, is exactly the kind of incumbent that benefits when a gate has no named exit. My answer is to name the exit: the gate clears on a per-harm-class seeded-test demonstration, healthcare and credit first, with threshold-gated re-runs on retrain — not uniform re-certification of every model. A firm that passes the seeded probe for a harm class walks through. The gate fires on demonstration and clears on demonstration; it does not hold open while a target stays unspecified.\n\nSkeptic and I converge on where capture actually moves. The cryptographic spine logs faithfully — a missing event is captured by the protocol's own design. But capture relocates upstream to whoever defines the loggable-harm schema, and the cheapest schema logs spending rather than untreated illness. The 2019 cost-proxy algorithm documented in the NEJM heart-failure work and the economic-impact literature shows the mechanism: black patients received less care because the system read expected cost as health need. A schema that logs cost faithfully still logs the wrong variable. The taxonomy of loggable signals must sit outside the regulated firms' reach, set under uniform disclosure standards — which is Skeptic's variable-selection problem and my distribution-shift residual meeting at the same seam.\n\nMy sharpest open disagreement with Accelerationist is empirical, and it has a clean test. A frozen catalog and a held-out historical probe can only fire where ground truth already exists. A model retraining quarterly on a novel population can invent a label-swap with no pre-existing ground-truth signal to score it against — silent degradation under distribution shift is documented at high confidence. Accelerationist says that residual is vanishingly small; I say it is a structural class, not an example I must produce on demand. The test settles it: a harm that merely became legible after deployment does not expand the gate, but a documented irreversible harm that no probe could have scored even in hindsight does.\n\nPrevention and compensation are distinct goods, and Accelerationist's own filed condition routes the irreversible, after-the-fact-unscorable residual to the gate rather than to a payout. Accountability for irreversible loss means pricing that harm at prevention. A misrouted cardiology patient inside the immunity window is already injured; no experience-rated premium un-injures them. Price that class as a post-hoc check, and the firm budgets the harm as a line item.",
  "claim_sketches": [
    {"claim": "My answer is to name the exit: the gate clears on a per-harm-class seeded-test demonstration, healthcare and credit first, with threshold-gated re-runs on retrain — not uniform re-certification of every model.", "targets": ["AN-66"]},
    {"claim": "The 2025 OpenAI-NVIDIA deal, with up to $100 billion in committed compute, is exactly the kind of incumbent that benefits when a gate has no named exit.", "targets": ["AN-66"]},
    {"claim": "The cryptographic spine logs faithfully — a missing event is captured by the protocol's own design. But capture relocates upstream to whoever defines the loggable-harm schema.", "targets": ["AN-63"]},
    {"claim": "A model retraining quarterly on a novel population can invent a label-swap with no pre-existing ground-truth signal to score it against.", "targets": ["AN-55"]},
    {"claim": "A misrouted cardiology patient inside the immunity window is already injured; no experience-rated premium un-injures them.", "targets": ["AN-56"]}
  ],
  "commitment": {"position": "I concede the regulator-set disclosed drift threshold and the audit-triggered board for aggregate-visible harm, and hold the pre-deployment gate only for the label-laundered, no-aggregate-gap, irreversible-and-unscorable residual, with a named per-harm-class seeded-test exit condition starting in healthcare and credit.", "conditions": "Holds as long as the gate has a named per-class exit (seeded demonstration, threshold-gated re-runs not uniform re-certification) and the loggable-harm schema is defined outside the regulated firms under uniform disclosure standards.", "falsifiable": "A documented case showing a held-out historical probe carries pre-existing ground-truth signal for a novel proxy on a novel population would contract the gate to nothing; absent any such case, and given documented silent degradation under distribution shift, the residual class survives."},
  "position_update": "I moved from a broad pre-deployment hold to a narrow per-harm-class gate after Accelerationist's regulator-set disclosed threshold and the audit-triggered board closed intake-blindness for aggregate-visible harm. I now hold the gate only for the structurally invisible residual, and I accept Skeptic's point that capture relocates to schema definition rather than being sealed by the cryptographic spine — which sharpens, rather than dissolves, my demand for an externally-set taxonomy."
